            <ArticleTitle>Current management of varicose veins.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>414-26</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Problematic varicose veins are estimated to occur in up to 30 million Americans and may be symptomatic and/or unsightly. The majority of symptomatic varicose veins occur in the lower extremities and can result in significant circulatory disease. This problem is more common in women as a result of pregnancy and child bearing. Cosmetic treatment for varicosities is best achieved with a variety of sclerosing procedures.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
